{
  "description": "Audit streams of anonymous ring transfers, one case per audit key and layout: commitment (class 4, two published inputs, both notes of the ring, no exit), commitment_exits (the same key with an exit), commitment_pair (class 4, three published inputs) and entry (class 8, two published inputs, the second a default-ring note, with an exit). Encodings, fixed inputs, layout, the blinding and the stream as in audit-disclosure-delivered.json. A ring output's owner tag is a free 32-byte view tag, the auditor reads its record and never opens its scheme 11 body. Every input belongs to the sender, owner Poseidon(owner identity of sender_key, sender_nullifier_pk), its data hashes zero, its commitment the UTXO hash under input_tree_id with ring id ring_id for a ring input and 0 for a default-ring input. envelope_plaintext = tx_viewing_sk || evidence. Commitment key evidence: be32(commitment of input i) per published input, entry key evidence: sender_key || sender_nullifier_pk || (be32(commitment) || u64be(amount) || be32(asset) || be32(blinding)) per published input. record_plaintext: a ring output owner_key || be32(asset) || u64be(amount) || be32(nullifier_pk), a dummy 104 zero bytes, an exit be32(asset) || u64be(amount) || be32(nullifier_pk). The auditor rebuilds every output from its record and its blinding and checks output_hash, a ring output's mint the held asset whose hash_bytes(asset_address) is the disclosed asset. Under the commitment key the auditor takes the sender as the owner of input 0 among the notes it opened before, and opens every input by the full hash the evidence names. Generated by sdk-libs/client/tests/disclosure_vectors.rs.",
